# Internal working docs — kept local; origin is PUBLIC.
# resubmission_plan.html holds reviewer strategy, journal/APC decisions and
# co-author coordination notes. A copy lives outside the repo at
# ~/Documents/projects/_plm_choice_internal_backup/.
/docs/NEXT.md
/docs/resubmission_plan.html
/docs/talks/
/docs/lrz_setup.md
/docs/manuscript_changes.md
/revisit/

# Conference poster sources — large binaries, not part of the code release
/docs/ismb_poster/

# Large binaries / data artifacts
*.h5
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.npy
*.ai
*.parquet

# Manuscript / Drive exports. A 42.7 MB Google Drive export of the MANUSCRIPT folder sat
# untracked AND unignored in the repo root for six weeks (removed 2026-09-15, verified
# byte-identical to _plm_choice_internal_backup/manuscript/plm_choice/ first). Origin is
# PUBLIC and linked from the preprint, so one `git add -A` would have published the paper
# drafts and a journal cover letter. Ignoring the class, not just that one file.
*.zip
*.docx

# The manuscript workspace is a NESTED PRIVATE REPO (github.com/tsenoner/plm_choice_publication).
# This repo is PUBLIC and linked from the preprint; the paper text, the reviewer responses and the
# master plan must never land in it. Ignoring the directory means git never offers it to `add -A`,
# and the nested .git means even a forced add would store a gitlink rather than the files — two
# independent barriers, which is the point. Edit the paper in manuscript/, commit it there.
/manuscript/
